        "intro": "The co-creation spheres represent three possible situations of consulting perceived value co-creation in the AI era (S1, S2, S3), alone or in combination. All three are located within the joint sphere of value co-creation (Grönroos & Voima, 2013).\n\nWithin this framework, the orchestration of co-creation situations is not fixed: it is dynamic and temporal, and the three situations may occur within the same phase of a consulting mission. S1/S2/S3 is an observation framework, not a managerial prescription.\n\nS1 constitutes the interpretive anchor of the observation system, making it possible to detect signs of AI-driven reconfiguration.\n\nManifestations of R, P and C in S2 and S3 (with AI) are understood by contrast with those observed in S1 (without AI), within the same mission. The analysis focuses on intra-phase variations, that is, moments when the S1, S2 or S3 situation changes while the mission phase remains constant. These intra-phase variations are considered the most discriminating units of analysis in the observation framework.",
